The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s inner display uses a complicated, multi-layer structure that Apple says will hold up to wear and tear.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/apple-iphone-duo-display.jpg" alt="" width="1553" height="874" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063648" /><br/>
There are 10 ultrathin layers in total, including a nano-textured cover layer made from a custom polymer that Apple says is up to 40 percent stiffer than "other materials used in the industry," which presumably means other foldable devices.<br/>
<br/>
Apple added high-strength glass above and below the folding display panel, along with a titanium plate at the bottom of the stack. Custom adhesives "allow the layers to glide past one another like the pages of a book, relieving bend stress," according to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
The exterior nano-texture layer's finish is meant to reduce glare and minimize the visibility of the crease, and a scratch-resistant coating covers the nano-texture layer.<br/>
<br/>
The outer display is protected by Ceramic Shield 2 like the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> models, while the back of the iPhone has Ceramic Shield. The inner display gets the custom polymer cover instead of Ceramic Shield.<br/>
<br/>
